## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design privacy-preserving, scalable PCA in federated, non‑IID environments with streaming updates and edge constraints. It probes local imputation, secure aggregation, drift detection, and robust evaluation under limited communication.

## Key Concepts
- Federated incremental PCA and rank-k SVD
- Local imputation and standardization
- Secure aggregation for global basis
- Drift detection via explained variance and reconstruction error
- Handling non‑IID data with weighted updates

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: federated PCA update flow
function federatedPCAUpdate(siteBatch) {
  const X = imputeAndStd(siteBatch);
  const {U,S,Vt} = onlineSVD(X, currentBasis);
  publishSecureSum(Vt);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you set thresholds for drift vs. false alarms in production?
- What failure modes are likely if a site drops out or data becomes highly non‑IID?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to combine nonlinear PCA with streaming data, GPU acceleration, and production latency constraints in a high-throughput setting.

## Key Concepts
- Kernel PCA via random Fourier features
- Incremental SVD in RKHS
- Streaming imputation and normalization
- Drift detection and adaptive component retention
- Translating loadings into governance alerts under latency pressure

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo streaming kernel-PCA core
function processBatch(batch){
  const Z = mapToRF(batch.features); // random Fourier features
  const upd = incrementalSVD(Z, batch.mask);
  const comps = computeLoadings(upd);
  if (driftDetected(comps)) updateComponentPolicy();
  emitAlertsFromLoadings(comps);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate RK feature approximation quality in production?
- How would you handle non-stationary drift with changing feature distributions?
